<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE HEADLINE CASE: after an edit, starting PLAYBACK in the edited region must
  play the material that belongs at the playhead — not a fragment from some
  other position.

  The user's repro was exactly this and nothing else: with tracks nested inside
  a group, edit a clip, hit play somewhere near the edit, and the first second or
  so is audibly WRONG — recognisable material, from the wrong place. Every audio
  assertion this suite owned was blind to it twice over:

    * they are position-BLIND. RMS, peak and f0 all pass on the right material
      played from the wrong offset. (Closed by the position fixture + the
      assert-source-position verb.)
    * they are render-only, and a RENDER is a different consumer of the graph
      than playback. The only backend a headless run could use was NullBackend,
      whose startOutput() sets a flag and never calls the render callback — so
      AudioEngine::pullBlock, the readahead frontier, the seek-on-start and the
      stale-page fallback had NO automated coverage at all. (Closed by the
      capture backend + dump-playback-capture.)

  This case is the first one to assert on audio that came out of the PLAYBACK
  path. It plays in real time into memory, writes the recording out, and decodes
  the recorded stream position by position.

  ================================================================= arithmetic

  All numbers are multiples of the encoding's 4096-frame block, because the
  decoder resolves to a block: a window that straddles a source block boundary
  lights two bins and is reported as ambiguous rather than as an answer. Keeping
  the split, the move, the locator and every window on the block grid is what
  makes the expectations exact instead of approximate.

  Fixture test_position.wav: 187 blocks = 765952 frames = 15.96 s @ 48 kHz,
  dropped at timeline 0 on the NESTED lane (path 0,0 — a track inside a folder,
  as in the repro).

    edit:  split at        393216  (8.192 s)  -> head [0,393216)  src = t
                                                 tail [393216,765952) src = t
           move tail to    491520 (10.24 s)   = +98304 (2.048 s) later
                                              -> tail [491520,864256) src = t - 98304
           gap            [393216,491520)     -> silence, 2.048 s of it

    pass 1 (bakes pages, exercises playback START before the edit):
           locator 98304 (2.048 s), play until 147456 (3.072 s), stop.
    pass 2 (the assertion pass, playback START inside/around the edit):
           locator 245760 (5.12 s), play until 573440 (11.94 s), stop.

  CAPTURE ALIGNMENT. The recording begins when the backend's pump starts, i.e.
  at playback start, so captured frame f is timeline frame 245760 + f. Measured
  on this machine: leading silence is ZERO frames and the recording is exactly
  as long as the playhead travelled (327680 frames), over 9 runs across
  SMARAGD_REVAL_WORKERS in {default, 0, 16}. The case does not DEPEND on that:
  the first content assertion sits 8192 frames in and carries a tolerance of
  8192, so up to two blocks of startup slop are absorbed explicitly rather than
  by luck. Everything the case discriminates is ~98304 frames away, so the
  budget costs no strength.

  MIN CONFIDENCE 1.5, not the default 3.0. A momentary underrun (the pump is
  paced by a real-time clock and does not wait for the readahead — deliberately)
  leaves a short zero gap inside a window, which leaks energy into the other
  bins and drags the best/runner-up ratio down. The argmax is still the right
  block; demanding 3.0 would turn a dropout into a POSITION failure and blame
  the wrong thing. One such run was observed at SMARAGD_REVAL_WORKERS=0
  (confidence 2.27, correct best guess).

  TWO LEGITIMATE ANSWERS IN THE MOVED REGION. Proposal 16 lets playback serve a
  stale-but-frozen page while an edit is absorbed, so a window over the moved
  tail may legitimately decode either the POST-edit source (t - 98304) or the
  PRE-edit one (t). Both are listed; a decode to any THIRD position is the bug
  this case exists for, and the failure message names the frame it decoded.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="playback_start_after_edit_position">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>            <!-- 0: becomes the folder -->
    <add-track index="-1"/>            <!-- 1: gets nested into it -->

    <add-sample trackPath="1" filePath="../test_position.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <!-- Nest it: the clip now lives on lane 0,0, one level inside a group,
         which is the structure the repro was reported on. -->
    <reparent-track source="1" destParent="0" destIndex="-1"/>

    <!-- Pass 1: real playback well before the edit region. This is not
         scene-setting — it starts the engine, bakes pages through the readahead
         and leaves a warm state chain, which is the state the reported bug
         appeared from. -->
    <set-locator position="98304"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead position="147456" minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="20000"/>
    <toggle-playback play="0"/>

    <!-- The edit: split at 8.192 s, move the tail 2.048 s later. -->
    <split-clip clip="0,0,0" splitTime="393216"/>
    <move-clip clip="0,0,1" destTrack="0,0" startTime="491520"/>

    <!-- Pass 2: start playback 3 s BEFORE the split and play through the split
         point, the gap and into the moved tail. -->
    <set-locator position="245760"/>
    <toggle-playback play="1"/>
    <wait-playhead position="573440" minAdvance="4096" timeoutMs="30000"/>
    <toggle-playback play="0"/>

    <!-- The recording, written with the same 16-bit PCM writer a render uses.
         minFrames is the last window's end: a short recording must be reported
         as a transport failure here, not decoded as silence three lines down. -->
    <dump-playback-capture filename="playback.wav" minFrames="315392"/>

    <!-- ============ 1. before the edit: the IDENTITY mapping ============
         capture f -> timeline 245760+f -> source == timeline (head is unmoved).
         The first one is the leading-silence budget (see the header). -->
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="8192"
                            expectSourceFrame="253952" tolerance="8192"
                            minConfidence="1.5"/>
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="40960"
                            expectSourceFrame="286720" minConfidence="1.5"/>
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="98304"
                            expectSourceFrame="344064" minConfidence="1.5"/>
    <!-- timeline 389120: the last whole block before the split at 393216. -->
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="143360"
                            expectSourceFrame="389120" minConfidence="1.5"/>

    <!-- ============ 2. the gap the move left behind: SILENCE ============
         timeline [393216,491520) -> capture [147456,245760). Nothing may play
         here: not the head (it ends at the split), not the tail (it starts
         2.048 s later), and not a stale pre-edit page — pass 1 never played
         within 245760 frames of this region, so nothing here was ever frozen
         with the pre-edit content. -->
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="163840"
                            expectSilence="true"/>
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="196608"
                            expectSilence="true"/>
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="229376"
                            expectSilence="true"/>

    <!-- ============ 3. the moved tail: post-edit OR pre-edit ============
         capture 245760 -> timeline 491520 = the moved clip's FIRST frame, the
         most sensitive point in the case: post-edit source 393216, pre-edit
         source 491520.
         capture 262144 -> timeline 507904: post 409600, pre 507904.
         capture 311296 -> timeline 557056: post 458752, pre 557056.
         Anything else — a neighbouring page, the head's material, the block
         that used to live at this timeline position before the SPLIT — is the
         wrong-position bug, and the rejection message names the frame. -->
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="245760"
                            expectSourceFrameAny="393216,491520"
                            minConfidence="1.5"/>
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="262144"
                            expectSourceFrameAny="409600,507904"
                            minConfidence="1.5"/>
    <assert-source-position filename="playback.wav" startFrame="311296"
                            expectSourceFrameAny="458752,557056"
                            minConfidence="1.5"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <!-- After the reparent only the folder is top-level. -->
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
